    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_clean_endpoint_picard_two_projection_socle_frame",
    "title": "Clean-endpoint Picard two-projection socle frame",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "reciprocal finite-pushforward direction",
    "statement": "For P_*=(x_0,S), the fibre quotients A_0=Q(z;x_0)/S and C_0=Q(S;X)/(X-x_0) are the positive-modification socle directions under the two finite projections. Serre duality maps them to evaluation at S and x_0. Consequently both pushforwards have the unique-section splittings O+O(1-rho)+O(-rho)^(m-2) and O+O(1-m)+O(-m)^(rho-2), and the marked point supplies an explicit domain-Veronese direction for the Hankel interface.",
